  "fig": "hhfig0",
  "gloss": "<b>e</b> is your eye height above the water, <b>d</b> the distance to the target, <b>R</b> the Earth's radius. Light leaves your eye, grazes the surface at the horizon distance <b>d₀</b>, and carries on straight; by the time it reaches the target it has climbed <b>H</b> above the water there. Everything below H is behind the bulge. On a plane there is no bulge and no horizon: <code>H = 0</code> for every e and every d, with no free parameter to tune. That is a sign difference, not a magnitude difference.",
