  "html": "<div class=\"srcs reading\"><b class=\"h\">Further reading</b> <div class=\"note\">Not cited above, and no claim on this tab rests on it — listed because it is what you would read next, or because it lets you redo the measurement on data this page did not choose.</div> <ul> <li><b>Andrew T. Young — <em>Sunsets, mirages and the green flash</em> (San Diego State University).</b> The reference pages on how much a real atmosphere can and cannot hide, by the author of the refraction work already cited elsewhere on this page. The right place to go before deciding that any particular hidden-height claim is refraction.</li> </ul> </div>",
